<div id="q-docs-metadata" class="question">
<h3>3. What metadata and documentation (for example the methodology of data collection and way of organizing data) will accompany the data?</h3>

<div class="answer">
<p>List of data to be published is given in Section 5, Question 10 and 11. This also includes information about repositories where the data can be found. Information about data types used is given in Section 1, Question 2.</p>

{# Metadata specifications #}
{% if data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications | length > 0 %}

    {% if data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications | length > 1 %}
        <p>In our {{ globals.projects }}, {{ data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications | length }} different approaches to metadata description will be applied to ensure the proper documentation and discoverability of research data.</p>
    {% elif data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications | length == 1 %}
        <p>In our {{ globals.projects }}, a single shared approach to metadata description will be used to ensure consistent documentation and discoverability of all research data.</p>
    {% endif %}

    <ul>
    {% for metadata in data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications %}
    <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5em;">

        {{ macros.datasetIntro(metadata, "metadata specification", data.dmp.datasets) }}

        {# Standard Metadata Specification #}
        {% if metadata.isStandardMetadata._value is sameas true %}
        <p>
            This metadata specification follows a standard metadata schema that supports harvesting and indexing{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.isStandardMetadata._path) }}.
            {% if metadata.standardMetadata.identifier %}
                {% if metadata.standardMetadata.identifier._raw %}: <a href="https://fairsharing.org/{{ metadata.standardMetadata.identifier._raw.id }}" target="_blank">{{ metadata.standardMetadata.identifier._raw.name }}</a>{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.standardMetadata.identifier._path) }}.
                {% elif metadata.standardMetadata.identifier._value %}: {{ metadata.standardMetadata.identifier._value }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.standardMetadata.identifier._path) }}.
                {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
        </p>

        {% elif metadata.isStandardMetadata._value is sameas false %}
        <p>
            This metadata specification does not follow any existing standard schema.
            {% if metadata.noStandardMetadata.reason._value == "no_standard" %}
            No standards are available in this project area{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.noStandardMetadata.reason._path) }}.
            {% elif metadata.noStandardMetadata.reason._value %}, because: {{ metadata.noStandardMetadata.reason._value }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.noStandardMetadata.reason._path) }}.
            {% endif %}

            {% if metadata.noStandardMetadata.metadataElements | length > 0 %}
                The following metadata elements will be captured as part of this custom schema:
                <ul>
                {% for element in metadata.noStandardMetadata.metadataElements %}
                    <li>{{ element._value }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(element._path) }}</li>
                {% endfor %}
                </ul>
            {% endif %}

            {% if metadata.noStandardMetadata.canBeHarvestedIndexed._value is sameas true %}
                The metadata will still be stored in a way that allows harvesting and indexing.{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.noStandardMetadata.canBeHarvestedIndexed._path) }}
            {% endif %}
        </p>
        {% endif %}

        {# Findability #}
        {% if metadata.isFindable._value is sameas true %}
            <p>Metadata produced according to this approach will be findable.</p>{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.isFindable._path) }}
        {% elif metadata.isFindable._value is sameas false %}
            <p>Metadata produced under this approach will <strong>not</strong> be findable{% if metadata.noFindableReason._value %} because {{ metadata.noFindableReason._value }}{% endif %}.</p>{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.isFindable._path) }}
        {% endif %}

        {# Connection to data #}
        {% if metadata.howConnectionToData._label %}
            <p>The connection between the metadata and the associated data will be ensured as follows: {{ metadata.howConnectionToData._label }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.howConnectionToData._path) }}.</p>
        {% elif metadata.howConnectionToData._value %}
            <p>The connection between the metadata and the associated data will be ensured as follows: {{ metadata.howConnectionToData._value }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.howConnectionToData._path) }}.</p>
        {% endif %}

        {# Language #}
        {% if metadata.language %}
            {% if metadata.language._raw %}
                The metadata will be provided in <em>{{ metadata.language._raw.name | lower }}</em> language.
            {% elif metadata.language._value %}
                The metadata will be provided in <em>{{ metadata.language._value }}</em> language.
            {% endif %}
        {% endif %}

        {# Availability of metadata #}
        {%- if metadata.isLicenseCC0._value is sameas true %}
            Metadata is available under the CC0 license.{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.isLicenseCC0._path) }}
        {%- elif metadata.isLicenseCC0._value is sameas false -%}
            {%- if metadata.noLicenseCC0Reason._value %} Metadata is <strong>not</strong> under the CC0 license, because: {{ metadata.noLicenseCC0Reason._value }}.{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.noLicenseCC0Reason._path) }}
            {%- else %} Metadata is not under the CC0 license.{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.isLicenseCC0._path) }}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if metadata.isAvailableAfterDataNotAvailable._value is sameas true %}
            Metadata will be available even after the data is no longer available{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.isAvailableAfterDataNotAvailable._path) }}
            {%- if metadata.howAvailableGuaranteed._value %}
            (we will do the following: {{ metadata.howAvailableGuaranteed._value }}){{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.howAvailableGuaranteed._path) }}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- elif metadata.isAvailableAfterDataNotAvailable._value is sameas false %}
            Metadata will <strong>not</strong> be available after the data is no longer available{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.isAvailableAfterDataNotAvailable._path) }}
            {%- if metadata.noAvailableReason._value %}
                (because: {{ metadata.noAvailableReason._value }}){{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.noAvailableReason._path) }}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
    </ul>
{%- else -%}
    <p>No metadata specifications have been defined for our {{ globals.projects }}.</p>
{% endif %}

{# Documentation Specifications #}
{% if data.dmp.sharedResources.documentationSpecifications | length > 0 %}

    {% if data.dmp.sharedResources.documentationSpecifications | length > 1 %}
        <p>In our {{ globals.projects }}, {{ data.dmp.sharedResources.documentationSpecifications | length }} different approaches to documentation will be applied to ensure the completeness, clarity, and discoverability of research outputs.</p>
    {% elif data.dmp.sharedResources.documentationSpecifications | length == 1 %}
        <p>In our {{ globals.projects }}, a single shared documentation approach will be used to ensure consistent description and discoverability of all research outputs.</p>
    {% endif %}

    <ul>
    {% for documentation in data.dmp.sharedResources.documentationSpecifications %}
        <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5em;">

        {{ macros.datasetIntro(documentation, "documentation approach", data.dmp.datasets) }}

        {# Description #}
        {% if documentation.description._value %}
            <p>
            This documentation approach will cover: {{ documentation.description._value | e }}.
            {{ macros.linkQuestion(documentation.description._path) }}
            </p>
        {% endif %}

        {# Additional included items #}
        {% set included_items = [] %}
        {% if documentation.includeMethodology._value is sameas true %}
            {% do included_items.append("methodological aspects of data collection") %}
        {% endif %}
        {% if documentation.includeDataValidation._value is sameas true %}
            {% do included_items.append("information on data validation procedures") %}
        {% endif %}

        {% if included_items | length > 0 %}
            <p>
            The documentation will include {{ included_items | join(" and ") }}{% if documentation.description._value %} to provide sufficient context{% endif %}.
            </p>
        {% endif %}

        {# Format #}
        {% if documentation.format._value %}
            <p>
            The documentation will be available in the following format:
            <strong>{{ documentation.format._value | e }}</strong>.
            {{ macros.linkQuestion(documentation.format._path) }}
            </p>
        {% endif %}
        </li>
    {% endfor %}
    </ul>
{% else %}
    <p>No documentation specifications have been defined for our {{ globals.projects }}.</p>
{% endif %}

{# Organisations - versions, file names #}
{% if data.dmp.sharedResources.organisationStrategies | length > 0 %}

    {% if data.dmp.sharedResources.organisationStrategies | length > 1 %}
    <p>In our {{ globals.projects }}, {{ data.dmp.sharedResources.organisationStrategies | length }} different approaches to data organisation will be applied to ensure the proper documentation and discoverability of research data.</p>
    {% elif data.dmp.sharedResources.organisationStrategies | length == 1 %}
    <p>In our {{ globals.projects }}, a single shared approach to data organisation will be used to ensure consistent documentation and discoverability of all research data.</p>
    {% endif %}

    <ul>
    {% for organisationStrategy in data.dmp.sharedResources.organisationStrategies %}
    <li style="margin-bottom: 1.5em;">

        {{ macros.datasetIntro(organisationStrategy, "file naming and versioning strategy", data.dmp.datasets) }}

        {# Relationships between files #}
        {% if organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isRelationshipsBetweenFiles._value is sameas true %}
            We will keep the relationships between data clear in the file names.{{ macros.linkQuestion(organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isRelationshipsBetweenFiles._path) }}
        {% endif %}
        {% if organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isMetadataEmbedded._value is sameas true %}
            All metadata elements embedded in file names will also be included in the formal metadata to ensure completeness and consistency.{{ macros.linkQuestion(organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isMetadataEmbedded._path) }}
        {% elif organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isMetadataEmbedded._value is sameas false %}
            Metadata embedded in file names will not necessarily be included in the formal metadata.{{ macros.linkQuestion(organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isMetadataEmbedded._path) }}
        {% endif %}

        {# Uses folder system  #}
        {% if organisationStrategy.usesFolderSystem._value is sameas true %}
            We will use a folder system to organize the data{% if organisationStrategy.folderSystemStrategy._value %}: {{ organisationStrategy.folderSystemStrategy._value }}.{% else %}, but no specific folder system strategy has been provided.{% endif %}{{ macros.linkQuestion(organisationStrategy.usesFolderSystem._path) }}
        {% endif %}

        {# Agreement on file naming convention #}
        {% if organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isAgreementOnFileNamingConvention._value is sameas true %}
            A project-wide agreement on file naming conventions and versioning for this data is in place{{ macros.linkQuestion(organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isAgreementOnFileNamingConvention._path) }}
            {%- if organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.agreementOnFileNamingConvention %}
                    ({{organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.agreementOnFileNamingConvention._value}}{{ macros.linkQuestion(organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.agreementOnFileNamingConvention._path) }})
            {%- else -%}, but no specific convention has been provided{%- endif -%}.
        {% elif organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isAgreementOnFileNamingConvention._value is sameas false %}
            No project-wide agreement on file naming conventions and versioning is in place.{{ macros.linkQuestion(organisationStrategy.fileNamingConvention.isAgreementOnFileNamingConvention._path) }}
        {% endif %}
        <p>

        {# Versions #}
        {%- if organisationStrategy.dataStorageSystemOrganisations|length > 0 -%}
            <p>
            Updates and versioning of data are managed according to the following strategy:
            <ul>
            {%- for dataStorageSystemOrganisation in organisationStrategy.dataStorageSystemOrganisations -%}
                {%- if dataStorageSystemOrganisation.storageSystem or dataStorageSystemOrganisation.versioningStrategy -%}
                <li>
                    {{ dataStorageSystemOrganisation.storageSystem._label if dataStorageSystemOrganisation.storageSystem and dataStorageSystemOrganisation.storageSystem._label else dataStorageSystemOrganisation.storageSystem._value if dataStorageSystemOrganisation.storageSystem else '<em>Unknown data organisation type</em>' }} ~ {{ dataStorageSystemOrganisation.versioningStrategy._label if dataStorageSystemOrganisation.versioningStrategy and dataStorageSystemOrganisation.versioningStrategy._label else dataStorageSystemOrganisation.versioningStrategy._value if dataStorageSystemOrganisation.versioningStrategy else '<em>Unknown versioning strategy</em>' }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorageSystemOrganisation.storageSystem._path) }}
                </li>
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
            </p>
        {%- endif -%}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
    </ul>
{%- else -%}
    <p>No file naming and versioning strategies have been defined for our {{ globals.projects }}.</p>
{%- endif -%}

</div>
</div>
